+  <body>
+    <a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to content</a>
+    <nav>
+      <div class="shell nav">
+        <a class="brand" href="#top">Verification redesign</a>
+        <div class="links">
+          <a href="#before-after">Before / after</a
+          ><a href="#local">Local loop</a> <a href="#authority">Authority</a
+          ><a href="#migration">Migration</a>
+        </div>
+        <button class="theme" id="theme" type="button">Theme: auto</button>
+      </div>
+    </nav>
+    <main id="main">
+      <header id="top" class="shell">
+        <p class="eyebrow">Monitoring monorepo · Phase 0 plan</p>
+        <h1>Remove the queue. Keep the quality bar.</h1>
+        <p class="lede">
+          Replace the mandatory local gate with direct package feedback and
+          hardened existing CI. Add no app, cloud project, scheduler, task
+          graph, or verdict store.
+        </p>
+        <div class="facts" aria-label="Current baseline">
+          <div class="fact">
+            <strong>96,688</strong><span>raw counted control-plane lines</span>
+          </div>
+          <div class="fact">
+            <strong>24.7 min</strong><span>median local gate request</span>
+          </div>
+          <div class="fact">
+            <strong>25</strong><span>registered worktrees at snapshot</span>
+          </div>
+          <div class="fact">
+            <strong>0 sec</strong><span>target shared local wait</span>
+          </div>
+        </div>
+      </header>
+
+      <section id="before-after">
+        <div class="shell">
+          <div class="section-head">
+            <h2>One large local control plane becomes three small stages.</h2>
+            <p>
+              The current system detects many risks. Its orchestration, shared
+              state, and process recovery now dominate local work.
+            </p>
+          </div>
+          <div class="compare">
+            <article class="system old">
+              <p class="eyebrow">Before · mandatory local gate</p>
+              <h3>Every push enters a shared machine queue.</h3>
+              <div class="flow">
+                <div>Edit and commit</div>
+                <div>Pre-push hook enters gate</div>
+                <div>Map paths and reserve shared resources</div>
+                <div>Run checks, journals, drains, and recovery</div>
+                <div>Push, then run overlapping CI</div>
+              </div>
+              <div class="chips">
+                <span class="chip">routing engine</span
+                ><span class="chip">coordinator</span
+                ><span class="chip">run.lock</span
+                ><span class="chip">freshness state</span
+                ><span class="chip">process drains</span>
+              </div>
+              <div class="proscons">
+                <ul class="list good">
+                  <li>Broad feedback before push</li>
+                  <li>Shared-resource containment</li>
+                  <li>Strong generated-drift coverage</li>
+                </ul>
+                <ul class="list cost">
+                  <li>Cross-worktree waiting</li>
+                  <li>Cloud timeouts</li>
+                  <li>Large Bash and test surface</li>
+                  <li>Overlaps CI</li>
+                </ul>
+              </div>
+            </article>
+            <div class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</div>
+            <article class="system new">
+              <p class="eyebrow">After · staged verification</p>
+              <h3>Local feedback is direct. CI owns the merge verdict.</h3>
+              <div class="flow">
+                <div>Pre-commit formats staged files</div>
+                <div>
+                  Author runs affected package commands at a coherent checkpoint
+                </div>
+                <div>Push starts immediately</div>
+                <div>
+                  Existing fixed CI fan-out runs affected jobs in parallel
+                </div>
+                <div>
+                  Review, exact-head readiness, merge consent, and live proof
+                  remain
+                </div>
+              </div>
+              <div class="chips">
+                <span class="chip">no local selector</span
+                ><span class="chip">no pre-push check</span
+                ><span class="chip">fixed CI jobs</span
+                ><span class="chip">fail-closed aggregate</span>
+              </div>
+              <div class="proscons">
+                <ul class="list good">
+                  <li>No shared local queue</li>
+                  <li>Fresh runner isolation</li>
+                  <li>Small, traceable architecture</li>
+                  <li>Same review and deployment proof</li>
+                </ul>
+                <ul class="list cost">
+                  <li>Some failures arrive after push</li>
+                  <li>Path filters need strong fixtures</li>
+                  <li>Hosted runner cost needs a ceiling</li>
+                </ul>
+              </div>
+            </article>
+          </div>
+        </div>
+      </section>
+
+      <section id="local">
+        <div class="shell">
+          <div class="section-head">
+            <h2>Local checks run at named moments.</h2>
+            <p>
+              The trigger table, not agent discretion, defines the required
+              checkpoint. CI remains required merge evidence.
+            </p>
+          </div>
+          <div class="moments">
+            <article class="moment">
+              <b>Every commit</b>
+              <h3>Format staged files</h3>
+              <p>
+                Keep the Trunk formatter only. Do not add package commands,
+                generation, or browser work.
+              </p>
+            </article>
+            <article class="moment">
+              <b>Coherent checkpoint</b>
+              <h3>Check affected packages</h3>
+              <p>
+                Run direct lint, typecheck, test, codegen, React Doctor, build,
+                and browser checks when their named trigger applies.
+              </p>
+            </article>
+            <article class="moment">
+              <b>Every push</b>
+              <h3>Start CI now</h3>
+              <p>
+                Pre-push does not fetch, route, lock, wait, or create freshness
+                state.
+              </p>
+            </article>
+          </div>
+          <div class="scenario">
+            <h3>Example: a dashboard page with indexer changes</h3>
+            <ol class="steps">
+              <li>
+                <strong>Regenerate contracts</strong
+                ><span
+                  >Run indexer codegen when schema, config, ABI, entry point, or
+                  reachability changes. Run dashboard codegen for query
+                  consumers.</span
+                >
+              </li>
+              <li>
+                <strong>Check both packages</strong
+                ><span
+                  >Run each affected package's lint, typecheck, and CI-aligned
+                  local test command. Indexer test measured 191.5 seconds and
+                  needs optimization.</span
+                >
+              </li>
+              <li>
+                <strong>Check the page</strong
+                ><span
+                  >Run <code>dashboard:react-doctor:diff</code>, build the
+                  route, and verify route, console, interaction, and auth states
+                  in a browser.</span
+                >
+              </li>
+              <li>
+                <strong>Use broad CI</strong
+                ><span
+                  >CI runs coverage, Knip, dependency checks, full React Doctor,
+                  Playwright, size checks, generated variants, and the
+                  aggregate.</span
+                >
+              </li>
+            </ol>
+          </div>
+          <div class="callout">
+            <strong>Measured exception:</strong> Governance Watchdog uses
+            <code>test:unit</code> as its normal author checkpoint. Its generic
+            <code>test</code> alias requires a service on
+            <code>localhost:8080</code>.
+          </div>
+        </div>
+      </section>
+
+      <section id="authority">
+        <div class="shell">
+          <div class="section-head">
+            <h2>Reuse existing CI. Harden its authority.</h2>
+            <p>
+              Keep one required <code>CI / ci</code> aggregate, Code Quality,
+              Sentry suites, Vercel, and Vercel Preview Comments.
+            </p>
+          </div>
+          <div class="contract">
+            <article class="card">
+              <h3>Required pull request path</h3>
+              <ul>
+                <li>Fixed jobs and pinned path filter.</li>
+                <li>
+                  Unknown and control-plane paths select all conditional checks.
+                </li>
+                <li>
+                  Closed-world aggregate rejects failed, cancelled, missing, and
+                  unexpected results.
+                </li>
+                <li>PR jobs restore protected-main caches but never save.</li>
+                <li>
+                  Automated review, feedback ledger, exact-head readiness, and
+                  human merge consent remain.
+                </li>
+              </ul>
+            </article>
+            <article class="card">
+              <h3>Immutable no-skip audit</h3>
+              <ul>
+                <li>
+                  Workflow definition comes from protected <code>main</code>.
+                </li>
+                <li>
+                  Dispatch inputs are PR number, full source SHA, and full base
+                  SHA.
